WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:06.610
Satoshi and Go went to the Galar Region
to investigate the mystery of Daimax.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.920
The two got separated in the forest,
and both ran into mysterious Pokémon.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:18.240
After that, Satoshi went with Dande
to stop the rampaging Daimax Pokémon,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.910
while Go went with Sonia
to search for clues to the legend.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.750
What awaits each of them
at their respective destinations?

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.770
Underground Energy Plant, Knuckle City

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:10.790
I’m so sick of this!
Underground Energy Plant, Knuckle City

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.300
I’m so sick of this!

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.280
It’s heavy, it’s hot,
and I’m all sweaty!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.780
Why do we have to do this?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.040
We’ve got no choice.
Sakaki’s orders, meow.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.800
True. It’s for our righteous evil.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.900
Right, meow!
Yeah!

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.750
Hey, you! Quit slacking!

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:38.090
Are you okay?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.180
Well... I guess...

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.570
Ms. Sonia’s driving sure was <i>something.</i>

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.640
Look at this, Go.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.320
Turf Town Geoglyph

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.560
That’s Turf Town’s geoglyph?

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.100
They say it depicts the legend of Galar.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.700
Let’s see...

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.390
When the Galar Region
was engulfed by a black vortex,

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.400
gigantic Pokémon rampaged.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.760
Then a lone hero wielding
a sword and shield appeared,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.130
and quelled the raging beasts.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:18.840
And you’re investigating the connection
between that legend and Daimax, yeah?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.610
Yeah. It’s my grandmother’s
homework for me.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.790
What does this geoglyph look like to you?

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.190
Gigantic Pokémon rampaging, I guess?

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.200
Is that the vortex?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.440
Could be.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.690
Say, Go... Don’t you think
that seems a lot like the current situation?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.950
Now that you mention it...

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:48.800
Perhaps the black vortex that brought about
the disaster, the Black Night...

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.540
...is about to appear in Galar again?

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.290
A black vortex...
The Black Night...

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:01.480
I thought I could figure something out
by coming here...

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.890
It looks like what happened back then.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.250
I once met Lugia.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.390
Lugia?! Whoa, that’s incredible!

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.160
The clouds formed a vortex back then, too.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.130
Maybe vortexes form whenever
legend-tier Pokémon show up?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.150
So the Black Night might be connected
with some crazy powerful Pokémon or something.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.040
Good point...
Go, this could be a real breakthrough!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.470
Come to think of it,
the first time we came to see Mr. Dande fight,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.970
I saw a massive Pokémon in the clouds.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.450
Maybe that one
has something to do with this!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:51.780
Intel was that this plant
hid the strongest, evilest Pokémon...

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.890
But where is it?

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:13.730
Chairman Rose, should I halt the injection of
Galar particles until the hangar has been strengthened?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.990
Is this not incredible, Olive?

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.590
So much energy is flowing
that we can’t control it all.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:26.310
The Black Night... The disaster that once
pushed the region to the brink of destruction...

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:32.550
It will be revived as Mugendaina,
the savior of Galar’s future.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:37.830
That’s it.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.960
The strongest, evilest Pokémon!

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.730
We’ll catch it for sure, meow!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:46.110
Ah... I see.
Don’t let them out of your sight.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.090
Very well, ma’am.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.490
Continuing purs—

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.720
M-Ms. Sonia...

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.130
Sorry... I did it again.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:02.840
By the way, Go,
where were you headed?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.010
Brassie Town. To go see someone
named Professor Magnolia.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.960
Huh... So we’re going
to the same place, then.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.910
Professor Magnolia
is my grandmother.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.600
Do you see it, Satoshi?

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.870
What is that?

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.300
Sekitanzan. Kyodaimax form.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.480
Coal Pokémon. Rock/Fire type.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.040
Flames hotter than 2,000 degrees
burn in the massive furnace within its body.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.500
Here we go. Stay alert!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.540
Got it!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.900
Ms. Sonia, what are these photos?

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:48.260
They’re four tapestries
we found in the Knuckle City vault.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:52.190
“Two youths gazing at the sky.”

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.530
“A disaster occurs...
The two bewildered youths.”

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:03.060
“The youths looking on at the
sword and shield that stopped the disaster.”

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:07.530
“The youths being crowned.”

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.210
It’s said that they tell the story
of the birth of Galar.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.530
Mind telling me what you think?

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:18.170
The same two people
are in all the tapestries.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:22.780
Did these two stop the Black Night
and were then crowned kings?

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.950
In which case,
there wouldn’t be one hero but two?

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.830
You think so?

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.300
I was thinking the same thing, too.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.930
But there was only one
hero statue in the stadium.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:41.020
Yeah. Over the years, people may have
made mistakes retelling the legend.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.640
Then...

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.540
Could there be other mistakes, too?

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.380
It’s certainly possible.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.260
All right...
I’m really getting excited!

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.890
I’ll report to Grandmother,
pass her test,

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:56.470
and become a Pokémon Professor!

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:59.550
...Yeah, right.
No way it’ll go that well.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.040
Grandmother is crazy strict.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.170
Why do you want to be
a Pokémon Professor?

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.790
Part of it is wanting to be
with Grandmother, but...

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.330
Mostly because of Dande, I guess?

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:14.550
Mr. Dande?

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.560
Dande and I are childhood friends.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:23.520
We both loved Pokémon
and dreamed of becoming strong trainers.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.400
When we were younger,

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.490
I taught him about battling...

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:33.920
But after he made his trainer debut,
it became clear real fast that he was a natural,

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.550
and before I knew it, he was the Champion.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.580
Try as I might, there’s
no way I can beat Dande in battle.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.550
So I thought I’d try working with Pokémon
in an entirely different way.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.900
Drapult! Dragon Arrow!

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.300
Gänger! Shadow Ball!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.740
Gänger! Psychokinesis!

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.700
The longer this takes,
the more damage it’ll cause.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.700
Satoshi, let’s finish it quickly!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.710
Yes!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.260
Drapult! Dragon Dive!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.170
Gänger! Shadow Ball!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.450
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.820
Gänger, return!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:57.530
Come back, Drapult!

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.250
You messed up the mine!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.120
You maniac!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.190
Never come back!

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.420
Get out of here!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.670
Cut it out!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.420
It’s not Sekitanzan’s fault!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:25.290
Remarkable! I knew I could depend
on the strongest Champion...

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.560
...and the young trainer
who has his respect.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.150
Chairman Rose?
Why are you here?

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.800
I just happened to be here
for an inspection.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.400
Then I heard about the incident
and came as fast as I could.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:40.100
Allow me to introduce you.
This is Chairman Rose of Macro Cosmos,

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.460
the company behind development
and supply of energy for all of Galar.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.930
He took notice of me
when I started out as a trainer,

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.290
and raised me.
I owe him a lot for that.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:49.880
Oh, I’m...

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.490
Satoshi, yes?

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:53.820
Dande told me about you.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.180
He said you showed
great promise as a battler.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.680
I have wanted to meet you.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.300
I-It’s a pleasure...

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.930
Chairman Rose.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:07.680
Do you still not know why the
Daimaxed Pokémon are running rampant?

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:12.850
I did look into it extensively,
but I couldn’t find a clear answer.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.460
Is this a threat to Galar...

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.940
...or is it...

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.200
...simply a trial
necessary for our future?

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.930
We need to do something fast.

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:28.430
At this rate, the lives of
Galar’s people and Pokémon will crumble.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.910
I agree!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:30.840
Satoshi.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:34.710
The Pokémon aren’t rampaging
because they want to, either!

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:39.480
How about a dinner
to commemorate our meeting?

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.640
I’ll treat you to plenty of
Galar’s most famous dishes.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.220
Famous dishes?!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.870
It’s a good opportunity.
Go ahead and join him.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.620
I’ll help fix the mine.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.900
I’ll help, too!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:58.930
Brassie Town

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:00.870
Professor Magnolia’s lab!
Brassie Town

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:01.820
Professor Magnolia’s lab!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.010
Researching legends
is pretty exciting, huh?

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.660
You think so?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.940
Yeah! Seeing or hearing
about new Pokémon...

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.420
...makes me want to find
and catch even more!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:18.400
It’s kinda like my world expands
every time I learn something new...

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.010
Or like I’ve taken the future in hand!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.140
I know, right? You might make
a good Pokémon Professor!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.010
Professor, huh?

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:32.020
But first I gotta fulfill my dream
of catching every Pokémon!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.870
Wow... What a dream!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:38.650
All right... I won’t give up!
I <i>will</i> become a Pokémon Professor!

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:39.590
Yeah!

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:45.660
What’s that?!

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:49.910
A meteor?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.900
Amazing! It’s...

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.580
A Wishing Star.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:58.340
They are said to fall into the hands
of those who bear earnest wishes.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.370
Grandmother!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.460
Professor Magnolia!

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.050
You came from Professor Sakuragi’s institute?

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.530
Is he doing well?

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:08.220
Yes.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.470
I came because I wanted
to learn more about Daimax.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:17.100
I see. There are still
many things we do not know...

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:21.270
But what we do know is that
a special power which only exists here in Galar...

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:25.190
...is linked to the
Pokémon Daimax phenomenon.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:28.440
We call this power Galar particles.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.620
Galar particles...

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:34.930
Have you ever seen Pokémon
Daimax in the Wild Area?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.500
Yes, I have.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.090
Galar particles are found within
the red lights that are released...

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.530
...from special Power Spots.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:49.730
They bring out the power
from within Pokémon and trigger Daimax.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.670
Power from within Pokémon...

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.450
And further research has revealed...

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:59.030
...that the Wishing Stars
falling from the sky...

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:02.960
...likewise contain Galar particles.

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.860
That meteor from earlier?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:11.200
Wishing Stars are capable of
attracting and drawing in Galar particles.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:16.850
I thought that making use of that capability
should enable us to control the gigantification of Pokémon,

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.130
and so I...

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.850
...cooperated with Chairman Rose
from Macro Cosmos,

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:25.010
and together, we succeeded
in developing Daimax Bands.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:26.860
That’s awesome!

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:28.300
And on that note...

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.800
Ta-daah! A present!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.560
I did some work on
the Wishing Star we just found!

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.270
A Daimax Band?!

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:40.840
It’s better to have one
if you’re gonna travel through Galar, right?

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.070
Thank you!

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:50.440
But why can Pokémon <i>only</i>
grow giant in the Wild Area or in stadiums?

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.320
The Power Spots.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:57.030
Daimax can only be used
at Power Spots.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:58.710
I see.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:02.690
Galar particles conceal much potential.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:09.470
Together, Chairman Rose and I researched
how to turn that power into energy.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.760
However...

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:14.100
Did something happen, Grandmother?

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.340
No.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:20.600
In any case, Sonia, I hope you
haven’t forgotten your homework.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:25.110
Please show me the results
of your research into the legend.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:25.750
Of course!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.240
I see...

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:40.710
There were two heroes,
and the Black Night was caused by a Pokémon...

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:46.850
A truly fascinating discussion.
You did well, Sonia.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:52.060
I got some help
from you, too, though.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.940
Way to go, Ms. Sonia!

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:57.010
But I cannot yet say
that you have passed.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.310
Where are the sword and shield
from the legend?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.010
How was the disaster prevented?

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.800
You need to solve <i>all</i> the mysteries.

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:09.530
Figured as much...

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:12.450
See? She’s really strict, right?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:16.090
But I wanna know
all about the legend, too!

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:18.160
We just gotta research it
thoroughly, yeah?

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.540
I suppose! Let’s give it our all!

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:26.570
Rose Tower, Shoot City

00:16:26.570 --> 00:16:27.920
This is great!
Rose Tower, Shoot City

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:27.930
Rose Tower, Shoot City

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.780
I love the view from here.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:35.400
Each and every one of these lights...

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:38.060
...houses countless lives and dreams.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:44.350
Galar itself is what lifted me out of poverty
and let me reach my current life.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.440
And I intend to do everything
within my power,

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:52.440
in order for this marvelous view
to last a thousand years.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.070
Oh, yes, Satoshi!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:17:00.550
I strive to guide
talented trainers like Dande...

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:01.700
What do you think?

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:03.680
Huh? Me?

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:07.960
I would support a strong trainer like you
with everything I have.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:12.990
Please stay by my side, as well,
and help me protect Galar's future.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:17.470
Oh, you’re so lucky, getting an offer like this
from Chairman Rose!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.220
I’ll pass.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:25.820
I wanna travel the world
with my own two legs,

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:28.160
meet loads of Pokémon,

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.230
and become stronger with them!

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.150
Is that so?
Very well. I understand.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.670
So nice and soft!

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.520
I wish Go could be here, too.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.750
Come to think of it,
didn’t he say we’d meet up later?

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:58.410
Incoming call from Go.
Incoming call from Go.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.300
Go?

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.870
Huh? You’re at
Professor Magnolia’s lab?

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:05.890
Yeah.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:12.440
I’m staying here for the night, and tomorrow
I’m going with Ms. Sonia to see the ruins in Lateral Town!

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.740
I see. I’ll come to
those ruins, too, then!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.570
Yeah! We’ll meet up there!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.320
Sure!

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:25.210
Knuckle City

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.960
Is it simply a trial
necessary for our future?

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:39.470
Does Chairman Rose
know something about the incident?

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.660
What is he doing
in the underground plant here?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.230
We’re off, Grandmother.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.560
Leave it to us, Professor!

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.440
Sonia.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.240
I need to tell you...

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:03.330
...why I broke off
my partnership with Chairman Rose.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:07.580
It was because I could sense
madness in his gaze.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:12.900
Chairman Rose will stop at nothing
to achieve his goals.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.680
These recent incidents of
Daimax Pokémon rampaging...

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:21.220
I have no proof,
but I have a bad feeling about this.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.110
And that is why, Sonia...

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:27.220
...you need to make haste in
uncovering the truth behind the legend.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:31.510
Don’t worry!
I’ll get to the truth, for sure!

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:32.350
Me, too!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.420
Weeds should be plucked
as soon as possible.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:44.240
Lateral Town

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.030
The Lateral Town mural...

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.460
It’s not really what I expected.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.880
It looks like it was painted
long after the time of the legend.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.980
It looks more like a doodle.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.510
Guess that’s a miss.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.110
Don’t worry about it!
Let’s go investigate the next ruin!

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.760
Can’t let you do that.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.390
You will come with us.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.400
Who are you?

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.890
Do as I say, and you won’t get hurt.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.470
You have to be kidding!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.110
Rabbifoot!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.600
If you won’t do as I say,
then I have no choice.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.780
Come forth,
Kyodaimax Dustdas!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:34.210
Kyodaimax?! Wait,
is this a Power Spot, too?!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.750
Ah! There’s Galar particles
coming from the mural!

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.740
Which means...

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.300
Come back, Rabbifoot!

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.970
Daimax!

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:51.310
We just gotta give it a go, yeah?!

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:03.560
All right! Now, do it, Rabbifoot!
Dai Burn!

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:14.670
Kyodai Stink!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.550
Rabbifoot!

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:39.870
Impossible!
There were statues behind the mural?!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:51.710
Mew!

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:52.460
Warrgle!

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:53.210
Runpappa!

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.000
Pawou!

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:54.750
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:55.540
Strike!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.340
Cresselia!

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.050
Amakaji!

00:21:57.050 --> 00:21:57.840
Jirachi!

00:21:57.840 --> 00:21:58.630
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.630 --> 00:21:59.420
Kibago!

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.170
Gonbe!

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:00.970
Bayleaf!

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:02.470
Freezer!

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:03.680
Zacian!

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:20.530
Mew!

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:21.320
Wooper!

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:22.070
Pachirisu!

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:22.900
Sunaba!

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.570
Absol!

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.450
Lunala!

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:25.240
Rabbifoot!

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.030
Tropius!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:26.780
Sunahebi!

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:27.660
Vibrava!

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:28.330
Burshamo!

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:29.080
Mokuroh!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:29.910
Rotom!

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:30.620
Mooland!

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:31.410
Dodorio!

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.120
Otosupus!

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:32.960
Swanna!

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:33.710
Nazonokusa!

00:22:33.710 --> 00:22:34.500
Samehada!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.290
Darkrai!

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:35.960
Iwanko!

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:36.790
Cortoise!

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:37.630
Scorupi!

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:38.380
Pippi!

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.130
Pinpuku!

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:39.880
Kunugidama!

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:40.630
Mankey!

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:41.460
Kimori!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:42.260
Ligray!

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:43.720
Rayquaza!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.430
Zamazenta!

00:23:07.140 --> 00:23:09.570
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:10.830
Go!

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:13.370
Rabbifoot! Dai Burn!

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:18.910
If Pokémon are exposed to that light,
they’ll start rampaging again!

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:20.970
I have to do something, Go!

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:24.400
Got it! I’ll go search for
Zacian and Zamazenta!

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:27.800
I can’t let you force
more innocent Pokémon to run wild!

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.610
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:32.630
Sword & Shield

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:34.150
“Mugendaina”
